Z||000000||snafus87||08-22-2001||04:36 PM||||Hi list.  I'm new to this list, so I thought I would post a question and brief intro.<P>First off, I have an 85GT with 179k miles.  It's "mostly" a fastback.  Its missing the smooth molding to finish around from the doors front, the trunk weatherstripping, and some repair/replacement body panels for those that are cracked/broken.<BR>The engine is in dire need of a rebuild/replacement (I was thinking 3.4, but I have not really checked into the $$$ or effort involved yet, so any info would be appreciated.)<BR>My problem is this:  I can't figure out how to get the amber turn signals wired in properly.  I have the haynes manual, and perhaps I'm just a idiot at reading the digrams, or perhaps I just need some help (maybe both).  I have the lights for the Pontiac wired in and working in conjunction with my parking lights.  I have to get to a junkyard here soon and get the necessary sockets for the lights (how many??).<P>I live in Lehighton, PA (if anyone is interested in helping in person, haha).<P>Anyway, thanks in advance for any help you all can give.<P>JT ||||reg||10
