Z||000002||snafus87||08-22-2001||04:50 PM||||When I got the rear body stuff from the junkyard, I took the wiring harness too, figuring I might be able to plug it in and get it to work, but it didn't.  I guess the pins are different.  The fastback harness (from an 86) is more or less useless now, I cut the sockets off that I needed (the ones that were salvagable) and spliced them into my existing 85 GT harness.  I'm not sure which would be easier, finding a complete GT harness and changing pins, or just wiring the turn signals into my existing one??||||reg||1
